# Ignore Visual Studio temporary files, build results, and
# user-specific files.

## Build artifacts
/bin/
/obj/
/**/*.user
/**/*.userosscache
/**/*.suo
/**/*.cache
/**/*.pdb
/**/*.mdb
/**/*.log
/**/*.vspscc
/**/*.vssscc
/**/*.docstates

## Visual Studio
.vs/
*.vcxproj.user
*.vcxproj.filters
*.csproj.user
*.dbmdl
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.cache
*.builds
*.pidb
*.svclog
*.userprefs

## Rider
.idea/
*.sln.iml

## ASP.NET Temporary Files
_ReSharper*/
*.DotSettings.user
*.DotSettings
.vscode/

## ASP.NET Scaffolding
ScaffoldingReadMe.txt

## NuGet
*.nupkg
# The packages folder can be ignored because of Package Restore
**/packages/*
# except build/, which is used as an MSBuild target.
!**/packages/build/
# Uncomment if necessary however generally it should be included in source control
# !**/packages/repositories.config

## Azure DevOps
.vspscc
*.vspcc
*.vssscc

## Visual Studio Code
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

## OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

## Rider
.idea/
*.sln.iml

## User-specific files
*.user
*.userosscache
*.suo
*.userprefs

## Other
*.db
*.bak
*.backup
*.tmp
*.temp

# JetBrains Rider
.idea/
*.sln.iml

# ASP.NET Core
appsettings*.json

# optional: keep appsettings.Development.json if configured in repo
# !appsettings.Development.json
